<div class="page-header">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="page-subtitle">Last updated: <%= Date.today.strftime("%d %B %Y") %></p>
</div>

<div class="content-wrapper">
  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Introduction</h2>
    <p>
      Hi, I'm Bram, the creator of TornManager. I respect your privacy and am committed to protecting your personal information. 
      This Privacy Policy explains how I collect, use, and safeguard your data when you use my service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Information I Collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you sign in, you provide your Torn API key. I securely store this key in my database and use it 
      exclusively to fetch your personal game data from Torn's official API. I require a minimum of Public Only level 
      permissions. Limited Access is required for stock portfolio features.
    </p>
    <div class="data-collection-cards">
      <div class="data-card">
        <h4>Your API Key</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Torn user ID, name, and level</li>
          <li>Stock portfolio information</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="data-card">
        <h4>Application</h4>
        <ul>
          <li>Personal statistics (stat enhancer usage, networth, energy drinks, etc.)</li>
          <li>Daily snapshots for historical tracking</li>
          <li>Xanax payments sent</li>
          <li>Faction grants received</li>
          <li>Faction member statistics (for tracked factions)</li>
          <li>Faction ranked war history and member performance</li>
          <li>Subscription expiration dates</li>
          <li>IP address</li>
          <li>Browser type and version</li>
          <li>Pages visited and features used</li>
          <li>Date and time of access</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>How I Use Your Information</h2>
    <p>I use the collected information for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Service Provision:</strong> To provide and maintain TornManager's features, including progress tracking, statistics analysis, and stock investment recommendations</li>
      <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> To verify your identity and maintain your session</li>
      <li><strong>Data Analysis:</strong> To track your personal progress over time and generate insights</li>
      <li><strong>Service Improvement:</strong> To understand how users interact with my service and improve functionality</li>
      <li><strong>Security:</strong> To detect, prevent, and address technical issues or abuse</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>I do not share, sell, or disclose your personal data to third parties.</strong> Your Torn API key 
      and game data remain private and are only accessible to you when logged in.
    </p>
    
    <p>I may disclose your information only in the following limited circumstances:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Legal Requirements:</strong> If required by law or in response to valid legal processes</li>
      <li><strong>Protection of Rights:</strong> To protect my rights, property, or safety, or that of my users or the public</li>
      <li><strong>With Your Consent:</strong> With your explicit permission for specific purposes</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      I implement appropriate security measures to protect your information from unauthorized access, alteration, 
      disclosure, or destruction. Your Torn API key is stored securely in my encrypted database and transmitted 
      over secure HTTPS connections.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. While I strive 
      to protect your data, I cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
    
    <h3>Data Location</h3>
    <p>
      Your data is stored on servers located in <strong>Helsinki, Finland</strong> (EU) within the Hetzner datacenter (hel1-dc2). 
      This means your data is subject to European Union data protection laws, including GDPR.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Data Retention</h2>
    <p>
      I retain your data as long as your account is active. Historical statistics are maintained to provide 
      long-term progress tracking and trend analysis.
    </p>
    
    <h3>Retention Periods</h3>
    <div class="tos-table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Data Type</th>
            <th>Retention Period</th>
            <th>Reason</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Personal stat snapshots</td>
            <td>Indefinitely (until account deletion)</td>
            <td>Long-term progress tracking</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Session data</td>
            <td>90 days</td>
            <td>Security monitoring and session management</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>API call logs</td>
            <td>30 days</td>
            <td>Debugging and usage monitoring</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Subscription records</td>
            <td>Indefinitely</td>
            <td>Payment history and subscription verification</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Profile data (name, level, etc.)</td>
            <td>Until account deletion</td>
            <td>Account identification and display</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Faction member statistics</td>
            <td>Until faction is removed from tracking</td>
            <td>Training compliance monitoring</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Faction ranked war data</td>
            <td>Indefinitely</td>
            <td>Historical war performance tracking</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    
    <h3>Your Data Rights</h3>
    <p>
      <strong>You can delete your collected data at any time</strong> through the Settings page when logged in. 
      You can also <strong>export all your data</strong> in JSON format from the Settings page. 
      Data deletion will permanently remove:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>All login sessions and session history</li>
      <li>All API call logs and monitoring data</li>
      <li>Your stored API key</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Your subscription status is tied to your Torn ID and will be preserved even after data deletion. 
      You can log back in anytime using your Torn API key, and your subscription time will still be active.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Your API Key Security</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Important:</strong> Your Torn API key grants access to your game data. Please follow these best practices:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Never share your API key with other individuals</li>
      <li>Only provide your key to trusted, transparent third-party services like TornManager</li>
      <li>Use a Public Only or Limited Access key (not Full Access) when possible</li>
      <li>Monitor your key usage at Torn.com using the 'key' → 'log' selection</li>
      <li>Revoke and regenerate your key if you suspect misuse</li>
      <li>You can pause or delete your API key at any time on Torn.com</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Torn API Usage & Compliance</h2>
    <p>
      TornManager is built in accordance with the Torn API Terms of Service. I use the Torn API to provide 
      gameplay enhancement features while ensuring fair play and data security.
    </p>

    <h3>API Data Usage Summary</h3>
    <div class="tos-table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Data Storage</th>
            <th>Data Sharing</th>
            <th>Purpose of Use</th>
            <th>Key Storage & Sharing</th>
            <th>Key Access Level</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Persistent - until account deletion</td>
            <td>Nobody (data is private to you)</td>
            <td>Track personal progress, statistics, and stock investments</td>
            <td>Stored securely / Used only for automation</td>
            <td>Public Only (minimum); Limited Access (for stock features)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    
    <h3>User API Calls</h3>
    <p>These endpoints are called using your personal API key to access your private data:</p>
    <div class="tos-table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Endpoint</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
            <th>Access Level Required</th>
            <th>Required</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/key/info</code></td>
            <td>Verify API key validity and access level</td>
            <td>Public Only</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/key/log</code></td>
            <td>Display your API key usage history</td>
            <td>Public Only</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/user/profile</code></td>
            <td>Fetch your name, level, and profile image</td>
            <td>Public Only</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/user/stocks</code></td>
            <td>Fetch your stock portfolio for dividend analysis</td>
            <td>Limited Access</td>
            <td>No</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>Application API Calls</h3>
    <p>These endpoints are called using the application's owner API key for public data and administrative tasks. Your personal API key is never used for these requests:</p>
    <div class="tos-table">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Endpoint</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/user/{id}/personalstats</code></td>
            <td>Fetch and track your personal statistics</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/user/{id}/basic</code></td>
            <td>Fetch basic info for payment senders</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/user/log</code></td>
            <td>Process Xanax subscription payments</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/faction/{id}</code></td>
            <td>Fetch faction name for subscription grants</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/faction/{id}/members</code></td>
            <td>Verify faction membership for grants; fetch member lists for training compliance</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/faction/{id}/rankedwars</code></td>
            <td>Fetch ranked war history for tracked factions</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/faction/{war_id}/rankedwarreport</code></td>
            <td>Fetch detailed war reports with member performance data</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/torn/stocks</code></td>
            <td>Fetch current stock prices and dividend info</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/torn/factionhof</code></td>
            <td>Display faction Hall of Fame rankings</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>v2/market</code></td>
            <td>Fetch points market prices for calculations</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>API Request Identification</h3>
    <p>
      All API requests made by TornManager include the comment parameter <code class="highlight-pulse">tmanager</code> to identify 
      them in your API key activity logs. This allows you to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Monitor TornManager's API usage through Torn.com's key log feature</li>
      <li>Distinguish TornManager requests from other services using your API key</li>
      <li>Track and audit all API calls made on your behalf</li>
      <li>Verify that only legitimate requests are being made</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can view all API requests at any time by visiting the 'key' → 'log' selection on Torn.com or 
      using TornManager's <%= link_to "Key Activity Log", key_log_path %> feature.
    </p>

    <h3>Compliance Guidelines</h3>
    <p>I follow all acceptable usage guidelines, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Never requesting Torn passwords from users</li>
      <li>Keeping API keys and data securely protected</li>
      <li>Optimizing API requests to minimize server load</li>
      <li>Respecting rate limits (100 requests per minute per user)</li>
      <li>Providing transparent disclosure of data usage and storage</li>
      <li>Not providing unfair competitive advantages</li>
      <li>Not selling or monetizing user data</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Cookies and Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      I use essential cookies to maintain your login session. These cookies are necessary for the service to 
      function and cannot be disabled.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Analytics:</strong> I use AppSignal for application performance monitoring and error tracking. 
      AppSignal collects anonymized performance metrics (page load times, error rates) to help me identify 
      and fix technical issues. This data does not include your personal information, Torn ID, or game data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>TornManager integrates with the following third-party services:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Torn API:</strong> The official Torn.com API is used to fetch your game data. Your information is shared with Torn's servers only when fetching updates via the API.</li>
      <li><strong>AppSignal:</strong> Used for application performance monitoring and error tracking. AppSignal receives only anonymized technical metrics (response times, error counts) to help maintain service reliability. No personal data, Torn IDs, or game information is sent to AppSignal.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>I do not sell or share your personal data with any other third parties for marketing or advertising purposes.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Age Requirement</h2>
    <p>
      TornManager is intended for users of Torn.com. In accordance with Torn's Terms of Service, you must be 
      at least 13 years old to use this service. I do not knowingly collect information from children under 13. 
      If you are under 13, please do not use TornManager.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      I may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. I will notify users of any material changes by 
      updating the "Last updated" date at the top of this policy. Your continued use of TornManager after 
      changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <h2>Contact Me</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how I handle your data, please reach out to me on Torn:
    </p>
    <p>
      <%= link_to "Bram [2728237]", "https://www.torn.com/profiles.php?XID=2728237", target: "_blank", class: "player-link" %>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
